# PDF Metadata Viewer — local configuration
#
# This prototype runs locally only: it reads a directory of personal documents
# and queries a private Notion database, so it is never deployed. Do not add it
# to a hosting provider's env vars.
#
# ─── Where to put these ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Config is read from two places, in precedence order:
#
#   1. This directory's .env      — prototype-specific overrides
#   2. The hub root .env.local    — shared across the hub app and every experiment
#
# Notion belongs in the hub root, alongside the app's own credentials, so it is
# configured once. You only need a .env here to override something — a different
# PDF directory, a test database, a non-default port.
#
# Caveat: .env.local is gitignored, so it does NOT propagate into git worktrees.
# When working in a worktree, copy it in or export the variables in your shell.

# ─── PDFs (prototype-specific — belongs here) ────────────────────────────────
# Directory to read. Relative paths resolve against the prototype root.
# Absolute paths are used as-is. Google Drive mounts are detected and reported
# with a specific error when the client is closed or files are not synced.
PDFS_DIR=pdfs

# ─── Notion (put in the hub root .env.local) ─────────────────────────────────
# People and organizations come from the Notion Entities database, where `Slug`
# is the stable join key. The generic tag vocabulary lives in
# config/tag-vocabulary.md and needs no configuration.
#
# Auth is shared with the hub app via @experiment-hub/notion-auth and resolves
# in this order:
#
#   1. NOTION_TOKEN — an internal integration token. The path that works on a
#      local machine and on Vercel.
#   2. The Replit connector — used automatically inside Replit. Its token is not
#      obtainable outside Replit, so local runs need NOTION_TOKEN.
#
# NOTION_TOKEN: create at https://www.notion.so/my-integrations, then share the
#   Entities database with the integration.
# NOTION_ENTITIES_DATA_SOURCE_ID: the Entities *data source* id, not the page or
#   database id. Fetch the database via the API and read it from `data_sources`.
# NOTION_TOKEN=
# NOTION_ENTITIES_DATA_SOURCE_ID=

# After a successful fetch the entity list is cached to .entities-snapshot.json
# so the app keeps working offline. That file is gitignored — it mirrors
# personal data.

# ─── OpenAI (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed for AI metadata suggestions. Every other feature works without it.
# Note the hub root uses OPEN_AI_API_KEY for its own purposes; this reads the
# conventional OPENAI_API_KEY, so set that one if you want suggestions here.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ─── Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to 3004. 3001, 3002, 3003, 3009, and 3010 are taken by other
# experiment prototypes.
PORT=3004
